  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Contribute to improving living conditions of populations affected by the floods in Rio Grande do Sul, Brazil.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The proposed intervention aims to support the federal, state and municipal governments in responding to the urgent needs of the most vulnerable population affected by the floods. More specifically, IOM will provide comprehensive management of five humanitarian collective centres for populations unable to return home. Management and operational support will include the provision of specialized technical staff, food, cleaning services, logistical services, as well as the promotion of protection, MHPSS, recreational activities, livelihood opportunities, among others.</narrative>
  </description>
